   |  P·R·O·G·R·A·M   D·E·S·C·R·I·P·T·I·O·N
_ _¦__________________________________________________ __ _
   :

    noC-Coupon allows sysops and other appointed users to EASILY make files
    downloadable  without any loss of credits to the leecher.  When used in
    conjunction  with noC-AutoFree, creating and maintaining free-downloads  :
    is MUCH less of a hassle.                                                ¦
                                                                             |
_ _:_________________________________________________________________________|__
   ¦                                                                         ¦
   |  I·N·S·T·A·L·L·A·T·I·O·N                                                :
_ _¦__________________________________________________ __ _
   :

    This program requires OS2.0 or greater.

    Simply copy the "noC-Coupon" drawer into "DOORS:" and mount the door as
    is  convention  with  your particular version of Ami/Sigma Express.  (A
    BBSCMD icon is provided for 3.xx users).

    Within  the  program  drawer there is a sample configuration file which
    should  be  edited,  called "noC-Coupon.config".  You may configure the
    following:

    ACCESS:
    Those  with  security levels equal to or greater than the number placed
    here  will  automatically  gain  access to  the program.  Omitting this
    parameter will mean only explicitly defined users may use noC-Coupon.
    (Example: "ACCESS=200")

    USER.[NUM]:
    You  may appoint up to 40 users to have access to this utility.  As you
    define  each user you must increment the number in [NUM].  Correct caps
    are not neccessary.  (Example: "USER.1=nocTurne" "USER.2=Jimmy Hoffa")

    COMMENT.[NUM]:
    Comments may be directed to individual users of the util when they use
    it.  (Example: "COMMENT.1=Dont make EVERYTHING free, man!" "COMMENT.2=
    Where the hell ARE you?")

    FREEDLTEXT.[NUM]:
    You may  define the  texts which will  denote a  free-download  in the
    file listing here.  Up to 20 may be set which the user may choose from
    during program usage.  They will  automatically be indented 35 spaces, 
    so keep them  under 45 chars in length.   ANSI codes may be used,  but
    if you do you should terminate the text with an ESC[0m sequence.

    (Examples: "FREEDLTEXT.1=>>>FrEe dOwnLOad, LeECHES!" 
               "FREEDLTEXT.2=>>>A FREE RELEASE FROM THG!" ) 
                                                                             ¦
_ _:_________________________________________________________________________|__
   ¦                                                                         ¦
   |  P·R·O·G·R·A·M   L·O·G·I·C                                              :
_ _¦__________________________________________________ __ _
   :

    When  first  run,  (after  typing  'COUP'),  the program will check the
    user's  security  level  in comparison to the access level required for
    entry  (if  defined).    If the user fails this check, his name will be
    searched  for  in  the configuration file.  The program will exit if he
    fails this as well.

    The user, if passing these security measures, will then be greeted with
    any COMMENT to him that may exist in the configuration file.  Following
    he  will  be prompted to enter the COMPLETE name(s) of file(s) he wants
    to  make  free-downloads.    Hitting  the  enter key on a blank line or
    entering 20 filenames will progress to the next stage.

    The user may then choose from the available FREEDLTEXT's or press Enter
    to abort the  entire operation.   The text he chooses  will be appended
    to the  file-description(s) of  the  files he  has chosen to make free.
    A request will be posed to the user verifying that he DOES in fact want
    to make the files he listed free.

    The  user will then be asked if he wishes the file descriptions altered
    to  denote the leechability of the files he entered.  If he chooses not
    to,  the  files  will be made free, but their descriptions will give no
    indication of this.

    If he DOES choose to, the UPLOAD file-listings will be searched for the
    descriptions  to  alter.    After  each  entry  is  found,   the edited
    description  with  the  appended  FREEDLTEXT  will  be shown.  Once the
    file-listing  has  finished  being  processed,  another   request   for
    verification  will be posed.  The user may opt to bail out, or continue
    and have the edited listing saved.

    The  last  stage  entails  the  actual  files  being   tagged   so that
    Ami-Express  will recognize them as being free.  The success or failure
    to change each file will be shown.

    Finally,  Coupon will ask the user if he wishes an EALL message be sent
    notifying users that these file(s) are free.   He may then enter a one-
    line tag which will be appended to the message.

    Of course during the course of program usage, the user will be notified
    of any errors that may take place, and they'll be handled appropriately. :
